  "behavior": [
    "Neutral opaque control origins retain only exact executable/parameter identity. Cold inspection requires a resolved, unfenced, nontransactional boundary; binding repeats identity and selected-layout validation without copying, inheriting requests or exchanging state.",
    "The shared realized-state validator now returns its layout contract error for absent geometry instead of panicking. Existing stateful construction and control exchange behavior remains covered.",
    "Native dense resident KV construction uses the same per-layer isolated copy worker/order as saved optional tables. Exact host publication moves the same buffer into fresh state with preserved arrays/scalars/layout/global offset and empty inference retention.",
    "Actual Metal copy facts plus dense P drive exact/-1 component admission. Tests cover nonzero padded/full, key-only, aliased, empty and all-stateless storage, saved source after original retirement, recovery roots, typed publication errors and escaped table/native charges.",
    "Frozen decoder pairs retain their original neutral origin through immutable duplication, including when copied through another model after the original model retires. Origin metadata does not retain model payload or replace complete source pins.",
    "Funded resume checks backend health/idleness, pool, original executable identity and saved parameter epoch before work; even a matching origin still rejects until fresh request/controller/input installation exists."
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "Root and independent native review found no remaining production blocker in the staged dense constructor or origin wiring; neutral control tests verify request/custody retention through existing exchange.",
    "One new native origin test initially tried to load a second model after a saved account reserved the shared domain. The intended ReservedWorkActive guard rejected loading. The fixture now finishes both model loads before constructing the saved account; only that test setup changed.",
    "Runtime, neutral and sampling checks preceded the test-only fixture correction; their selected production behavior was unchanged. The saved-copy check and subsequent native/build checks ran with the corrected fixture.",
    "The origin fixture uses actual bounded tiny Llama generation and copying. Dense component fixtures instead quote actual P plus isolated native N without claiming a future forward workspace. Parameter invalidation tests invoke the real identity-rotation operation, not a numeric parameter replacement."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "These are managed component payload and provenance results with existing descriptor/handle/allocator bookkeeping exclusions; they do not establish a total-process memory bound.",
    "Fresh decoder/sampler/input/controller composition, quote of the actual saved branch, new core preparation/context, local versus inherited prediction ordinals and failure-safe installation/readiness still require integration. Generic funded snapshot restore/fork remains rejected.",
    "Origin alone proves neither complete source inventory nor numerical correspondence of arbitrary supplied state. Closed native source construction and final bind must preserve those separate contracts.",
    "Hybrid/paged state, complete facade/controller/capture/ingress payloads and the full resident/host/disk/distributed/media/speculation matrix remain unfinished. The V4 lazy-helper loading gap is separate pending work.",
    "No new released-checkpoint, native distributed hardware or total-process peak-memory measurements were performed."
  ]
